Revision history for App-Shotgun

{{$NEXT}}
    - FTP and SFTP targets log their debug messages through the logger of
      the App::Shotgun object, so a logger given by the caller is respected
    - SFTP targets check the host key strictly: an unknown or changed host key
      ends the run within seconds with an error naming the host, instead of
      the connection stalling
    - Add the SFTP target option ssh_options ( -o values for ssh ) to set
      known_hosts or relax the host key check where it is wanted
    - Read the login of a target without username from ~/.netrc, so no
      credentials have to be given on the command line
    - Log every successful transfer to a file with --transferlog
    - Upload to all targets at the same time with --parallel instead of one
      target after the other
    - Build the file list from the source directory, including all
      subdirectories, with --filerecursive
    - Ship the example script with placeholder hosts and without credentials
    - Write the shotgun command line documentation: name, synopsis, a
      description of the upload order and a section for every option
    - Target types are checked against the known transports (FTP, SFTP) and
      loaded without a string eval, so a crafted target string can no longer
      run code
    - FTP upload: a file that cannot be read completely is now reported as an
      error instead of being closed as a successful, truncated upload
    - Update to @Author::GETTY plugin bundle
    - Move prereqs to cpanfile
    - Rewrite POD to @Author::GETTY PodWeaver conventions
    - Compose MooseX::Getopt as a role, drop the unused logger error handler
    - Add getopt and logger-warning regression tests

0.001     2011-05-17 05:11:32 Europe/Berlin
    - First release
